{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare","id":540746,"title":"Beast : What's your nightmare ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T00:54:49-07:00","id":540746,"title":"Beast : What's your nightmare ?","content":"So, with Beast we can play the game of &quot;which monster are you ?&quot; easily : just analyse your dreams and nightmares to find which Beast you could have become.<br /> <br /> Personnaly, I think I could be an Eshmaki. It's not my favorite family, if I could choose I would definitily go for Makara : I love all the stuff water-related, swimming in pool, sea, river or the like. But I never dreamed of drowning, water doesn't scare me a bit. For the others, I dreamed occasionnaly of being hunt by something and couldn't run anymore (Anakim), or realized suddenly I was naked in the street (Ugalu). But that wasn't the worst nightmares ever.<br /> <br /> Besides, I was always afraid of the monster under my bed. Or the monster under the stairs. Heck, the bogeyman under my bed that I saw in my dreams even has a name : Monsieur Ouest (Mister West in french, don't ask why &gt;&lt;). Being alone at home was my biggest fear, and even recently I awoke at night with the certitude of not being alone, and I had to check each doors and windows before going back to bed....<br /> <br /> Hence, if the homecoming was a real thing and I could make it, I certainly be an Eshmaki.<br /> <br /> And you, what's your worst nightmare ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T01:10:33-07:00","id":540766,"title":"","content":"I can't really think of my worst nightmare, though I had the recurring naked and teeth falling out ones when I was younger... So I'd be an Ugallu with the latter as a Nightmare if I had to stat myself out.<br /> <br /> I'm quite partial to the Eshmaki personally, I like the concept of something lurking in the dark, though I never had a nightmare involving anything like that. I've been on walks in the night and the fear has poked into my mind and also as many a child, I had a fear of the darkness in my bedroom when night came for I couldn't see if anything could come and 'get me', but never in actual sleep. I suppose whilst the Eshmaki cover that element of nightmares, it could make an actual Nightmare for an Ugallu (forgive my slight naivety over the named Nightmares, I've yet to read their full descriptions in the book atm) ^_^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T03:29:36-07:00","id":540833,"title":"","content":"well, usually when I have nightmares, it is not about some specific thing- there is just a.. presence. I usually don't see the monster or even the cause of my fear, I just know that it is there, watching, waiting. Something bad is going to happen, but I can't say what. I'm not sure if that is more of an Eshmaki, Anakim or Ugallu- I kinda think it is the first, considering that my big fear is silence, but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T05:11:06-07:00","id":541006,"title":"","content":"I'm not really sure which one I would be. As a kid I had nightmares about everything from killer clown dolls (Eshmaki) strangling me to alien abductions (Don't know what that would be) to bigfeet in the woods behind my house (Anakim (they are the giants, right?). Of course I wasn't really scared of the bigfeet in my dreams, so I guess Eshmaki.<br /> <br /> Also, my RL family is prone to prophetic dreams, so I wonder how to that would play into the homecoming, maybe an Eshmaki that represents the fear of the unknowable future?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T05:45:19-07:00","id":541019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=541006#post541006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure which one I would be. As a kid I had nightmares about everything from killer clown dolls (Eshmaki) strangling me to alien abductions (Don't know what that would be) to bigfeet in the woods behind my house (Anakim (they are the giants, right?). Of course I wasn't really scared of the bigfeet in my dreams, so I guess Eshmaki.<br /> <br /> Also, my RL family is prone to prophetic dreams, so I wonder how to that would play into the homecoming, maybe an Eshmaki that represents the fear of the unknowable future?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fear of Fate/Prophecy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T07:27:56-07:00","id":541155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=541019#post541019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fear of Fate/Prophecy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fear of fate would certainly be a good one for my mom, since she's the doom prophet of the family. Her prophetic dreams always predict bad things. She's predicted everything from a couple plane crashes to a guy she knew dying of a heart attack, to one of her ex-boyfriends dying. The thing is, she predicts these things the night before they happen, so it's often too late for her to stop them by the time she gets ready in the morning. So the fear of fate would be perfect for her.<br /> <br /> My estranged/abusive father ,weirdly enough, predicts happy stuff, like the time he saw the lottery numbers in a dream, but being the idiot he is, he didn't write them down and could only remember the first three numbers when he went to buy the ticket. He still won a few hundred dollars, but he would have won the whole thing had he got out of bed and wrote the numbers down instead of trying to wake my mom up to get her to write them down. He might represent the fear of the wicked being rewarded for their evil, if not to himself.<br /> <br /> I always felt it was weird that my mother, who is mostly a good person, predicts doom and gloom, while my abusive, bipolar, possible sociopath father predicts happy stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:00:21-07:00","id":541210,"title":"","content":"Makara: I'm not afraid of water or of drowning-hell, I <i>love</i> the water, and the ocean, and pools and lakes and rivers and...-but I'll be damned if there's not a recurring nightmare where I'm out at my family's lake house that I frequented when I was an adolescent, out on the water which is, for some reason, a muddy brown color while something drags my intertube around while I hang on for dear life. The feeling of powerlessness while something huge and beneath the surface tries to fling me off of my tenuous safety tube is chilling, and I always fall off and hit the water. Whereupon I wake up.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Makara Tyrant, easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:05:09-07:00","id":541226,"title":"","content":"My one consistent dream through out life is of falling. Ugallu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:54:28-07:00","id":541331,"title":"","content":"I have consistent dreams about being forced to watch while others are harmed, and one about flying/falling. So I'm probably Ugallu or maybe Anakim. I think the powerlessness in either prolly makes me a Tyrant too (my kids would say so).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T08:56:22-07:00","id":541333,"title":"","content":"I've had several vivid, recurring nightmares over my life, but the most recent one was genuinely quite terrifying in hindsight. It hasn't actually shown again, but it struck me hard.<br /> <br /> I'm in the backseat of a car. I don't know who's driving, because I can't see their face - nor can I open the windows or fiddle with the radio that was only giving out static. I arrive at my grandfather's windmill and house in the nearby mountain range, and notice how desolate it is. Everything around looks more than empty; it looks abandoned, haunted and chilly. There's no one I can see, and the only thing I hear is the wind. The sun is hidden behind gloomy clouds. Even the car is empty but for me, I notice. That is when, looking out the window, I see something. There, some distance away, is a thin, tall man. He might have been just a shadowy silhouette. He might have been wearing a suit and a top hat. Maybe it was both. It has a smile from ear to ear, and shaking, bloodshot eyes.<br /> <br /> He's found me. I remember panicking, but as I try to leave the car and run, everything is sucked towards it, like drawn by a crushing vortex. And then I was blinded and could feel myself being restrained, and I screamed.<br /> <br /> And then I woke up in cold sweat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-05-2015, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T09:18:24-07:00","id":541345,"title":"","content":"@YeOfLittleFaith : so much details, it's horrifying &gt;&lt; sounds like Anakim or Eshmaki <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T09:28:14-07:00","id":541352,"title":"","content":"It might not be the most frightening dream I've had, but the nightmare I get when I'm sick always sticks with me the most. I'm in an unfamiliar place, trying to get somewhere. (Maybe home, maybe just somewhere familiar, I don't really know.) The longer I walk, the more lost I get, and I can never manage to retrace my steps. I'm afraid that I'll never get find my way out, but I can't do anything but keep going forwards.<br /> <br /> Certainly sounds like the You Are Lost Nightmare to me. I can't really say what Family it evokes, since there's no actual antagonist to the dream, though I definitely used it as inspiration for that Slenderman Beast I've been making.<br /> Especially since I also get this fascination with &quot;the figure standing alone in the dark.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:10:58-07:00","id":541484,"title":"","content":"Reading the Nightmares, I for sure have had the <i>Flying and Falling</i> one... Usually followed by that really horrid feeling of waking up midway and that feeling (I don't know what it's called) when you're falling <i>down the bed</i>? Apparently wikipedia calls it Hypnic jerk... I noticed a few Adult Fears in there, not what I would call Nightmares, but fearful thoughts and ponderings, such as You are Alone and You Deserve This. So perhaps Nightmares can really be made from anything classed as a fear.<br /> <br /> I have had one or two <i>You Cannot Run</i> dreams more recently... Thankfully these come to end of my sleep patterns so I don't hold my breath too long... xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T11:16:10-07:00","id":541487,"title":"","content":"I have two nightmares that I have had since I was a kid. One is me waking up in my bed with an overwhelming sense of terror, jumping out, and running away. Only to have my ankle grabbed by something and being pulled back under the bed. Even when I had a mattress on the floor shortly after living on my own I had that dream. The worst part is trying to scream for help and no sound coming out. I never dared to look behind me.<br /> <br /> The second dream is of &quot;something&quot; in a large wooden chest. The wood was partially rotted and from the holes in it this thing would stare at me and laugh. And then the chest would rock violently as the thing tried to break out. <br /> <br /> But the most recent recurring dream is of me pulling me teeth out. So..., yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1110-unjustcustos","name":"UnjustCustos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T12:18:27-07:00","id":541558,"title":"","content":"As a child the most vivid recurring nightmare I had was of a swamp or marsh with this bleak lake of still water. Everything is in this grainy noir black and white, like an old movie. I'm stuck in the mud, and then I see the thick lake water begin to bulge upward. All I can see of what lay beneath it is a shadow ... and then I snap awake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T13:33:54-07:00","id":541640,"title":"","content":"I find the stuff to do with things crawling inside the body quite horrific... I can admit to having a fear of hosting parasites in my body... Noone wants to have something like intestinal worms inside them, for example... So the name <i>Infestation</i>, though it's an Atavism, not a Nightmare and is not actually about that but more becoming a human sized swarm of insects... I think that would make a powerful custom Nightmare... I suppose it would fall under <i>Bugs Everywhere!</i> but it's not about them crawling over and stinging and being visible... It's the dread that they're probably inside, feeding from the nutrition you take in and getting bigger... <i>And bigger</i>... Until they want to come out, through whatever orifice it cares too... *shudders*<br /> <br /> <i>You are Infected (Vampire)</i> is also a nasty one for the fear of catching an STD... The Sin-Eater Nightmares are also pretty resonant too. Someone's health failing them becomes a greater fear with age after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T14:08:30-07:00","id":541674,"title":"","content":"I'm not up to date on Beastly matters, but this thread sounds like fun.<br /> <br /> I haven't had many recurring nightmares on my life. But I've had a few particularly vivid ones.<br /> <br /> The first is when I woke up to find my house was somehow wrong, like the furniture had been moved around. I wander around a bit, and then various objects began to throw themselves at me, this particularly spiteful poltergeist effect continued until I woke up.<br /> <br /> The other was one where I woke up alone in someplace too dark to make out. I couldn't move or really do anything until a painfully bright light came charging towards me. I woke up when the light created into me.<br /> <br /> (Un) Fortunately, there's nothing beast like to work with in there.<br /> <br /> Edit: Looking deeper into it, I seem to have running themes of betrayal (often by inanimate objects), and painful lights. (Maybe something that has to do with those.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 06-05-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T14:11:12-07:00","id":541676,"title":"","content":"This idea has been niggling at me since I read the families. I conceptualize and have a nightmares like an Eshmaki, but I was treated growing up and well into my working life as something like the Namatru... I guess nightmares and dreamscapes take priority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T15:20:05-07:00","id":541740,"title":"","content":"As a child my only recurring nightmares were about being unable to speak. In all sorts of different situations, just nothing would come out.<br /> <br /> Now as an adult, I only ever have nightmares about friends, family or my wife being killed or taken from me in some other manner, and me failing to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> I'd say that's pretty Anakim, I dread the idea of being powerless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:11:08-07:00","id":541984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=541226#post541226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one consistent dream through out life is of falling. Ugallu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elaboration: I've had three variations of this dream going on in my life.<br /> <br /> The first is not actually falling, but it's similar in execution: I'm perpetually going down going down a spiral slide, usually in green-and-purple colors, surrounded by the infinite dark. Sometimes I find a desolate bottom, all soft pads and plush blocks, but it's not a place I want to stay-it's hauntingly empty. More common, I find a brass jetpack...somewhere, and I try flying up. Doesn't matter how fast I go, how long I do it-I never get back up, and I always run out of fuel. Other times I just climb, and eventually the slickness gets to me. When I was young, they'd always start with me going down it at the top, in a Peter Piper Pizza-esque place. I no longer dream of it.<br /> <br /> Around my teenage years, the narrative changed, but the idea was the same. I'm falling next to an endless brick wall, with nothing else but blackness. Sometimes, I'll scrape myself bloody and raw trying to get a grip, and I do, and I climb. Inevitably, I always slip, always lose strength. It keeps going.<br /> <br /> After Mummy came out, I occasionally get a variation where I'm falling next to giant, wet white something. THere's no gripping it, no hope of stopping the fall. I wouldn't want to risk it too much, anyways. It's very clear I'm falling next to a giant canine tooth.<br /> <br /> I have no fear of falling in real life. I took a jump once that could have careened me off a waterfall if I hadn't been lucky, and suffered nothing in response. I want to skydive. I think I might have control issues.<br /> <br /> And in relation, is there any surprise that my own rule with designing my character for the playtest was that chambers could only very rarely have ground? If ground? The Heart was nothing but the Hurricane of Night, a placid two-dimensional lake, and a barren white tree on it's edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T20:35:24-07:00","id":542074,"title":"","content":"I don't <i>think</i> I have nightmares - at least nothing I could use for Beast.<br /> <br /> Oh, I've had falling dreams (which end in dissatisfaction; <i>that</i> was the jolt at the bottom?), I had one dream drenched in dread (a robot was suffering an existential crisis. I wasn't in it), and there was one case where a spider crawled on my face while I was asleep and I dreamt a squirrel-thing came through my window and tried to suffocate me with its tail. All of them were one-offs.<br /> <br /> One of my <i>only</i> persistent &quot;sets&quot; of dreams are the ones where I'm in love. They're usually <i>really</i> sappy and mundane; cuddling up on the couch, meeting up with friends, having quiet talks where I realize that yes, they do indeed <i>love</i> me. I had one a few nights ago where I was on a vast, ornate train and I was just starting to flirt with the girl in a nearby cabin (maybe mine? It's a bit vague) - it felt like that feeling where you're <i>just </i>starting to get a crush on someone, that quietly happy <i>swelling</i> feeling. And then I wake up, and the realization that <i>none</i> of that is real hits me. The loneliness cuts like a knife.<br /> <br /> It depends - sometimes the realization is a gentle let-down, and sometimes I'm shaken to the core. Most of the time the girl in question looks <i>nothing</i> like anyone I know; heck, the people in those dreams tend not to be anyone I recognize. The <i>one</i> time one of those dreams included people I know involved one of my friends speaking to me on the side of the highway where his house <i>should</i> have been.<br /> <br /> He told me love would only result in me dying alone in the gutter. I believed him for days after waking up; the words in that ditch were utterly convincing, like they were <i>right</i>.<br /> <br /> If anyone can make a Beast character around that, I'd be happy to see them.<br /> <div align=\"center\">\u2022 \u2022 \u2022</div> <br /> The only other persistent theme in my dreams seems to be vast towers and places much larger than they should be. This is my happy theme, and tends to show up everywhere from beaches to pirate ships to city-centers to streets where smiling children are selling cake that makes you evil (<i>that</i> was a bizarrely entertaining dream.)<br /> <br /> That does sound like a Lair theme to me, actually. Hmm...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T21:57:28-07:00","id":542231,"title":"","content":"I'd call that a Makara? But not in relation to anything.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki touches on the big one in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T22:27:25-07:00","id":542274,"title":"","content":"A huge, raging whirlpool. I am a small child, standing on it's edge. I throw something in; I never see what it is until I let go. Usually it was a favorite toy, sometimes something else. It is always a painful shock, watching it hit the churning water and disappear. Then I notice something. It's the thing I threw in last time, spat back up by the abyss. Cool! Except when I get there, it's always filthy and broken and sad and I wish I hadn't noticed it.Then I have this moment of intense self loathing that carries me to the end of the dream. Makara with a hunger for Ruin, definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T09:23:59-07:00","id":543945,"title":"","content":"I have Anakim nightmares for sure. I'll have vivid dreams where I spend what feels like hours, maybe days, trying to escape from enemies too big and too scary to fight, and the dreams only end when I realize I can't get away and turn to fight anyway. Interestingly enough, once I do I find that I can win. The worst and most terrifying of them end with me getting so angry I shift into a lucid dream, and when I'm lucid dreaming and angry there's nothing I can't do. I once had a nightmare where the entire sky tried to crush me because I noticed it was the wrong color. The effort involved in just getting back to my feet was enough to snap me awake, but I fought the sky and won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:22:42-07:00","id":544059,"title":"","content":"Fear of showing up to class and realizing that there's a test today you didn't study for. I graduated 10 years ago, mind you, and I STILL get the dreams.<br /> <br /> Not sure how that translates into a Beast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T11:59:59-07:00","id":544118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=544059#post544059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fear of showing up to class and realizing that there's a test today you didn't study for. I graduated 10 years ago, mind you, and I STILL get the dreams.<br /> <br /> Not sure how that translates into a Beast</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a sense of powerlessness, which would be Anakim. So go ace that test and realize your true self as a giant, angry pencil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T12:19:51-07:00","id":544136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=544118#post544118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a sense of powerlessness, which would be Anakim. So go ace that test and realize your true self as a giant, angry pencil.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or as a oversized Giant made of quiz papers that constantly leaks bloody red ink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T09:59:56-07:00","id":643129,"title":"","content":"The last nightmare, the last dream I can remember, from when I was a kid. It was like a B-rated adventure horror movie.<br /> <br /> Originally I showed up in a jeep to an ancient ghost town (seemingly a mix of Pueblo style and Wild West buildings) hidden deeep inside the mouth of a gigantic cave in the shape of a Dragon's head. From here I was attacked by hordes of zombies and forced towards the back of the cavern, gore being spilled from the people who were with me. This leads to a large downward spiraling stairs made of natural stone, leading into the bowels of the earth, and lit only from below by what turns out to be sweltering pools of magma. and on the other side is an enormous portcullis made of solid wood. I still don't know why, but I suddenly thought it was a good idea to open it and as it pulls upwards, rows upon rows of demons (or what I think were demons) start to march out of the darkness within, that darkness moving outwards swirling with the light from the glowing magma. And deep within the darkness, are two glowing eyes...<br /> <br /> I didn't really wake up there but I did start dreaming lucidly, so it wasn't really the dream anymore. Usually I don't even remember having dreams, the fact that I remember this one so well is rather amazing.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'd say that if I were to put a Family to my nightmare it would probably be Anakim, Eshmaki, or Makara.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 08-31-2015, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T14:59:29-07:00","id":643440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=541333#post541333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> That is when, looking out the window, I see something. There, some distance away, is a thin, tall man. He might have been just a shadowy silhouette. He might have been wearing a suit and a top hat. Maybe it was both. It has a smile from ear to ear, and shaking, bloodshot eyes.<br /> <br /> He's found me. I remember panicking, but as I try to leave the car and run, everything is sucked towards it, like drawn by a crushing vortex. And then I was blinded and could feel myself being restrained, and I screamed.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>In hindsight, I've managed to put a solid face on my Horror! It's pretty much the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Babadook\" target=\"_blank\">Babadook</a> from the titular movie.<br /> <br /> Which is hilarious to me, because I had never even heard of the Babadook at the time. Only months after having that nightmare did I stumble upon some comments on the movie, which led me to look it up and watch some scenes online. Imagine my surprise when I find the monster an eerie visual match to the one I saw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T15:39:03-07:00","id":643474,"title":"","content":"Really, this is difficult for me, considering I apparently <i>don't</i> dream. At least, I don't appear to remember them. The few times I do remember myself dreaming, I've forgotten what they are by lunch. There's only a single dream I've ever kept. <br /> <br /> It happened when I was a kid; it was my birthday and we had gone to Disney, where we did some stuff at a fancy arcade place, and I guess I partied a bit too hard. In the dream, I'm alone on a roller-coaster, where the shtick is that the ride is entirely in this big tube that twists and turns, decorated by spiraling lined of blindingly bright lights in multitudes of colors, the same sort of pattern as a candy cane, but with a lot more colors and layers. I want off, but the ride is moving so fast I can't even scream, the force is pushing on my chest too hard, and the colors were glowing hard enough to hurt. Thankfully, my torment was ended when my mother woke my up because she was seriously concerned(rightly so, I think) that I was sobbing into my pillow as I slept.<br /> <br /> If I were to judge my Horror by this, I'd say I would be categorically Anakim. Not sure how I'd describe said Horror, but an Amusement Park that exists soley to make the victims feel overwhelmed and exhausted seems good Lair materiel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T17:10:31-07:00","id":643561,"title":"","content":"Dreams of being lost. Ugallu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T18:51:04-07:00","id":643681,"title":"","content":"About the only nightmare that really stays with me is:<br /> <br /> I start out somewhere normal. Maybe I'm talking to friends, maybe I'm listening to a prof in class, sometimes I'm walking outside.<br /> Now, I'm in the habit of running my tongue along my teeth constantly.<br /> Not super obviously, just a quick run when my mouth's closed.<br /> While I'm doing whatever normal thing I'm doing, and my habit kicks in, I notice one of my teeth is a little loose. Nothing big, but, as one can expect, I can't keep well enough alone.<br /> I wiggle it around. I find it gives me a weird, not <i>quite</i> painful feeling, more like an exposed feeling (?) in that little spot.<br /> Again, no biggie. Till it comes out. Straight up comes out. No pain, nothing attached. Like a book that just slips out from a tightly packed library.<br /> Now I'm trying to put it back. Without making it obvious to everyone around me I'm putting it back.<br /> That's when the others start getting loose. One by one they come out. The feeling spreads. That's not the worse of it, though they idea of not being able to feel my teeth any longer does start to freak me out (beyond the layer of worry that comes with your mouth literally falling apart).<br /> The worse is the looks everyone is starting to give me. They all start to look at me, not with worried looks, not with looks you'd expect from those 'where are my pants' dreams, but just blank stares. Like I'm something out of place. A curiosity that doesn't merit any real attention, but that's there for your viewing pleasure.<br /> I panic. I can't keep my mouth closed very well, and teeth start falling to the floor. While I'm scrabbling to pick them up and get out the door to... anywhere where I can put myself together, I notice my nails feel loose as well. Soon enough I'm starting to try and pick up teeth like using my hands like they'll fall apart with the slightest breeze. That's when the bones in my hands and feet start to feel stretched. Like someone is pulling them away from me, and the joints aren't completely in...<br /> <br /> It goes on like this for a while (the farthest I got was an eye popped out and I could see myself looking at myself, in a way that I think you can only do in a dream without throwing up). I usually wake up by the nail part, which is nice. Once the bones start going though, the people start picking up my parts.<br /> That makes it a little weird to look at your friends the next day, since you recall them picking up teeth and nails and skin like it was loose paper that fell on the floor. Something of absolutely no consequence.<br /> <br /> Quite the clich\u00e9 kinda dream, I admit, but I don't quite now where that puts me.<br /> I had thought Namtaru when I started typing, but Ugallu now seems the better fit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cThe good sleep better, but the bad seem to enjoy the waking hours much more.\u201d</b> -<i>Woody Allen</i> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":5322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","user":"Zimthehacker","date":".  bad paragraph spacing 08-28-2015, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","name":"Zimthehacker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T19:53:48-07:00","id":643707,"title":"","content":"Can Makara come from other kinds of depths, or just the fear of deep water?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T20:03:22-07:00","id":643708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=643707#post643707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Makara come from other kinds of depths, or just the fear of deep water?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other kinds of depths are explicitly viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T20:16:18-07:00","id":643713,"title":"","content":"Then Makara might work to fit my dreams of painfully bright lights and creatures just out of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T06:58:06-07:00","id":645370,"title":"","content":"My worst nightmares usually revolve around me, in some kind of fugue state, murdering everyone I like. Ofsome part of me <i>enjoying this, knowing I don't have to care anymore, ending the life of every family member, friend, lover, enemy, just so I won't have to care about anything or anyone</i>, and the rest of me screaming to stop. It's somewhere between helplessness, destruction, and the release of apathy. I'm not sure what Beast that would make me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T08:44:36-07:00","id":645439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=645370#post645370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My worst nightmares usually revolve around me, in some kind of fugue state, murdering everyone I like. Ofsome part of me <i>enjoying this, knowing I don't have to care anymore, ending the life of every family member, friend, lover, enemy, just so I won't have to care about anything or anyone</i>, and the rest of me screaming to stop. It's somewhere between helplessness, destruction, and the release of apathy. I'm not sure what Beast that would make me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds either Namtaru or Anakim to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T17:03:46-07:00","id":646105,"title":"","content":"Facing some terrible thing that no one else even notices. Namtaru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T17:51:22-07:00","id":646147,"title":"","content":"I've only had a three nightmares that I can remember. first was the running but not going anywhere dream pretty standard except I was always on my knees for some reason.<br /> <br /> One that I saw a few times was one where I was witnessing bad people going crazy and destroying everything.<br /> <br /> The last one is not one that was the main focus but was a secondary thing that kept happening was I would try to smile but I'd find it hard and it would keep twitching. The Nightmare for that would defiantly be Can't Smile Without You.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T07:40:41-07:00","id":646644,"title":"","content":"I know for a fact I'd be an Anakim. My nightmares have always focused on being weak and powerless. Often they involve me moving in slow motion, my body acting of its own accord, losing the ability to speak even when shouting at the top of my lungs, or whatever attacks I perform have little to no effect on my enemy. If I'm really unlucky, I'll have multiple symptoms in the same nightmare. Sure I've dreamed of all kinds of creatures attacking me or creepy situations I've been in, but the one constant that persists in my dreams is that I have no control over the situation or ability to defend myself.<br /> <br /> Side note, I'm one of those people who can feel pain in my dreams. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-31-2015, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T08:09:13-07:00","id":646728,"title":"","content":"When I was a child I had the nightmare of one of my stuff animals I didn't like coming to life with claws and teeth and trying to get me. Now I am not fluent on Beast yet still working on it. but which one would pose as children toys and try to kill people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T08:13:00-07:00","id":646752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=646728#post646728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I was a child I had the nightmare of one of my stuff animals I didn't like coming to life with claws and teeth and trying to get me. Now I am not fluent on Beast yet still working on it. but which one would pose as children toys and try to kill people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Probably an Eshmaki (fear of being alone / being destroyed), or maybe an Namtaru (fear of revulsion). <br /> <br /> The Eshmaki possibility is pretty obvious, you're playing with your toy and suddenly it tries to kill you.<br /> <br /> As for the Namtaru, there's a lot of people who are terrified of dolls, especially those fucking Madam Alexander ones!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T18:33:50-07:00","id":647521,"title":"","content":"I had a nightmare last night in which my girlfriend's overweight stepfather was dancing to the South African national anthem (as performed by a nearby chorus) and I grew increasingly terrified at my ability to play the guitar, which I <i>knew</i> I shouldn't be able to play (because I can't).<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I got nothing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T05:50:54-07:00","id":647902,"title":"","content":"My only recurring nightmare is me walking down the stairs of a very narrow castle tower when a huge Indiana Jones-style round boulder trap triggers and I have to run away from it, but I'm not fast enough. Usually wake up when it finally catches my back foot. Ugallu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T07:42:21-07:00","id":648016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoragoSolitude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/540746-beast-what-s-your-nightmare?p=647902#post647902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only recurring nightmare is me walking down the stairs of a very narrow castle tower when a huge Indiana Jones-style round boulder trap triggers and I have to run away from it, but I'm not fast enough. Usually wake up when it finally catches my back foot. Ugallu?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds more like Anakim. Ugallu implies some sort of exposure aspect, while what you're describe seems predicated on the fact that you can't run away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T22:13:28-08:00","id":786510,"title":"","content":"As a Child I had a recurring nightmare more like a sequential nightmare about a Jack O lantern headed scarecrow full of straw and everything with clawed hands and a Scythe...The first dream He chased me through a corn field, slashing at me as I woke up. The second he came in my bedroom window and attacked me and my older brother who shared a room..till my father burst in and hit it with some blunt object, I can't really remember( I was 4) and it escaped out the window...the third I was in the same corn field and came upon a cracked and rotting jack o lantern lying beside a crumpled pair of black pants and red and black flannel shirt the same the monster wore...Strange that my nightmare resolved itself...but by that...IDK Eshmaki?<br /> <br /> My most recent Horror, or at least strange dream Ive had I was in my Apartment(A fictionalized one) trying to sleep it was dark, and cold, and I kept hearing strange bumping noises coming from through the wall. For some reason at first I think ghost, then I Assume it is my neighbors making loud noises, so I go to ask them to keep it down, leave my apartment and go to the door beside mine. Now for some reason, instead of the normal little peep hole common to apartment doors that allow you to see outside the apartment, these doors had large round porthole windows like on the side of a ship, the doors were also made of metal. Anyway, I go to my neighbor's door and knock on it. When I look up into the porthole The entire apartment is filled with red liquid, which I knew to be blood but honestly it wasn't opaque enough to be blood. So i am looking into this apartment that is like a fish aquarium of blood, and floating there right in front of the porthole is a figure staring back at me, and my last thought before waking up was...I Think that is me in the blood staring back at me....Now I have no idea what family that is Esmaki for the noises, Namtaru for the blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Keep your Friends Close and your Enemies at Knife point.","edited":{"userid":10265,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10265-neksys","user":"Neksys","date":". 12-15-2015, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10265-neksys","name":"Neksys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10265_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T08:29:39-08:00","id":786735,"title":"","content":"Based on the recurring episodes of sleep paralysis I've been experiencing for as long as I can remember that always involve me being completely paralyzed and helpless and <b>awake</b> while a demon (its forms vary, but it's always the same demon) either sits on my chest or watches me from the ceiling of my room, I'm going to say I'd probably be an Anakim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T09:51:20-07:00","id":1451227,"title":"","content":"Across my entire life, only two dreams that I could feasibly classify as \u2018nightmares\u2019 have really stuck with me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The first occurred when I was somewhere around 3-5 years old (and considering my memory, it\u2019s both dumbfounding, and a testament to it\u2019s impact on me, that I\u2019ve been able to remember it so well for this long, considering how shoddy my memory is (I\u2019m 21 FYI)), I only experienced it once or twice (I think(?)) and it was actually rather basic; I, and a crowd of other people I was near the back of, were running like mad across a vast, seemingly infinite, \u2018plains\u2019/\u2018field\u2019 of grassy hills (Knolls? Hummocks? Whatever, they were most definitely <i>some</i> sort of small-ish hill) while a great, dragon-like monster/beast, like what you see in the crest of Whales, was chasing us. The dragon-monster was burning and eating people behind me in the crowd, getting ever closer with each kill. That\u2019s about as far as I got before I fell out of bed, though. I think I somehow managed to roll onto my side and started crudely mimicking my movements in my dream.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d probably peg it as that of an Anakim with a hunger for either Ruin (unlikely), or Prey (much more plausible).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second occurs more consistently, for a given value of such, but is much, <i>much</i> \u2018tamer\u2019 in comparison. Basically, it consists of me floating deep within the depths of an ocean that is simultaneously both warm and comforting, yet cold and disturbing. My dream-self instinctively recognizes as the Cosmic Ocean, that unreal, but true, yet sidereal Ur-Place from which all things originated, and to which all shall eventually return. Though floating at a 'depth' (for the ocean is both sea and sky) that would make the deepest parts of our seas look like nigh-completely dried out puddles in comparison, I can still see the night sky. All throughout, I'm get the consistent emotional impression of lamentation, sadness, melancholy and acceptance, alongside the mental thought-impression of these following Lines;<br /> <br /> &quot;A bottomless curse, a bottomless sea,<br /> source of all greatness, all things that be.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A bottomless curse, a bottomless sea.<br /> Accepting of all that there is and can be.&quot;<br /> <br /> For this one, I think that the Makara Family fits best, though I have little clue as to the Hunger. Collector, perhaps? Deities <i>know</i> that I'm a minor kleptomaniac when it comes to loose cash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 06-10-2021, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T15:54:12-07:00","id":1451918,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Necromancy.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" ta